  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Our Samsung combi microwave keeps whirring for a few minutes after it's finished and beeped, even with the door open. Old one never did that. Is the fan stuck on?"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "[Heading: Probably normal]\nThat is almost certainly normal behaviour. Most combi microwaves have a cooling fan that continues to run for several minutes after cooking finishes to cool down the magnetron and internal electronics. It often keeps running even if you open the door or press stop. As long as the noise is just a steady whirring from the vents (not grinding, scraping, or loud rattling) and it eventually stops on its own, there is no fault. You do not need to do anything; just let it run until it switches off."
  }
